                <pb facs="0542" n="440" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg440"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2126/322.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                        Furniss.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-11-27"><hi rendition="#italic">November 27,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Bacon informs Mr. Furniss that blockade and closing of ports held by
                    insurgents without previous notice and effective force will not be recognized
                    and that indemnity may be claimed for losses sustained by reason of refusal to
                    clear vessels for such ports.</p>
            </div>
